# South-west: Broken Pillar, the Noxious Lair, Dunemaul, Thistleshrub Valley ----------------------

turnin 3380
accept 3444
tip The Stone Circle is for a later guide: keep it.
accept 3161
do 3161 bg
tip Put on the Gahz'ridian Detector (a helmet): while you wear it, the buried ornaments show on the minimap as little piles of sand to loot. They lie all over the south of Tanaris and respawn quickly; the ogre ruins have the most.
do 82
tip The Centipaar insects fill the Noxious Lair, the hive west of Broken Pillar; about one in three drops parts. Stay on its edges: the swarmers call up lots of little adds (they look like critters) and draw others from far away, and every Centipaar thrashes.
do 97530 bg
do 5863
tip Gor'marok the Ravager waits alone in a shallow cave at the south end of the compound, visible from outside. Clear the ogres at its mouth first; he hits hard and uses Mortal Strike. Avoid the Dunemaul Warlocks if you can: their Curse of Thorns hurts.
do 97530
tip The bangle drops only from the ogres of the Dunemaul Compound itself, not from the two smaller ogre camps nearby.
do 3161 at 45.5,65.8
tip The richest ornament fields are the Eastmoon Ruins (around 46,65) and the Southmoon Ruins (around 40,73, fewer ogres).
do 2605 bg
do 3362
do 2605
tip Only the Thistleshrub Dew Collectors drop the gland, and only now and then. They share spawn points with the other Thistleshrubs, so killing those for Thistleshrub Valley brings more collectors.
accept 1560
tip Tooga stands at the north of Thistleshrub Valley (around 29,60) or near the crashed zeppelin (around 31,74), where he spawns before walking north. He has a long respawn: skip him if he isn't up. You can't take his quest while another timed quest runs.
tip Tooga has half an hour to get home, so do everything else first. He follows you on foot and slowly: walk. If something attacks, stop and kill it, or he stays behind to fight it.
do 1560 bg
accept 97540 at 41.2,54.3 late "Lead Tooga to the little pool in the Dunemaul Compound and take Oasis from him"
tip The pool lies in the middle of the compound, under a half-circle of red awnings. Tooga stops to swim in it: talk to him then. If he doesn't offer it there, look for it again when he reaches Torta.
turnin 97540 at 41.2,54.3 "Hand Oasis back to Tooga"
turnin 3161
tip Walk Tooga past Broken Pillar to hand in the ornaments on the way.
turnin 1560
turnin 95321
accept 95472
tip Tazzik's shirt goes back to Friz in Riverglades at the end of the guide.
turnin 97530
